  "note": "Election of the Enniskillen Borough Council, polled 18 September 1946; there was no contest (Belfast News-Letter, 5 September 1946, p. 3). The paper says fourteen Unionists, six Nationalists and a Labour candidate were nominated, but names only five Nationalists; the twenty it names are recorded, returned unopposed. The sixth Nationalist is not named in any source found: the Fermanagh Herald (7 September 1946, p. 5) reports the Nationalist selection, in which P. McNamee and J. Lynch replaced two who withdrew, but not the nominations. Wards are not given. Returned unopposed.",
  "correctionNote": "Citation corrected (w19-council-fix-west, Nov 2026): the list is in the Belfast News-Letter, 5 September 1946, p. 3 (the link pointed at an Irish News page that is not on the archive); read on the page image, which prints the Labour member as 'James Bradley' (recorded so, previously J. Bradley). The note's claim of an unfilled Nationalist seat is replaced by what the paper says."
